              <aside class="quote group-Roblox_Staff" data-username="Bogden" data-post="10" data-topic="2945587">
<div class="title">
<div class="quote-controls"></div>
<img alt="" width="24" height="24" src="https://doy2mn9upadnk.cloudfront.net/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/bogden/60/7477616_2.png" class="avatar"> Bogden:</div>
<blockquote>
<p>The current plan is to replace the dropdown entirely, so that when you click on the property, it would open the picker instead. Curious to hear what you like about the current dropdown over this option!</p>
</blockquote>
</aside>
<p>I might be influenced by having used Roblox for over 5 years but I eventually come to know the materials by name. Often to set a specific material for instance, I can just click on the dropdown, type “Me” (for Metal) and I don’t even have to look at the dropdown.</p>
<p>Having to manually search through a list of materials that is much less than the current condensed one seems like a hassle more than a blessing. However I am a scripter so I might not have as much of a need for visuals as people who solely do modelling/building</p>
